{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496121-alchemy-enchantment-and-the-resources-sanctum-background-for-sorcerers","id":1496121,"title":"Alchemy, Enchantment, and the Resources/Sanctum Background for Sorcerers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-02T12:44:48-07:00","id":1496121,"title":"Alchemy, Enchantment, and the Resources/Sanctum Background for Sorcerers","content":"So, since it is now explicitly stated that Alchemy and Enchantment are tied to the number of resources or sanctum dots a sorcerer/extraordinary citizen has, I was wondering what would be a good mark per dot for each level of Alchemy/Enchantment needed. PoP states 1 dot per each Alchemy or Enchantment level, which seems a bit stringent to me if an ST is running a chronicle where backgrounds are hard to raise or maintaining assets is difficult. M20: Sorcerer simply states that they should be tied, but gives no numeric description.<br /> <br /> I think if I were to run a game I would allow Sanctum or Resources 1 to allow Alchemy or Enchantment 1-2 dot creations, 2 to allow 3-4 dot creations, and 3+ to allow 5+ dot creations. I assume once you hit Resources or Sanctum 3, that you are capable of getting all of the resources necessary for your creations given enough time. What do you all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","user":"Starcomet","date":". 02-10-2023, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}